---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';

const link = 'text-forest underline underline-offset-4';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy: what this site records | OakFox"
  description="What oakfox.co.uk records when you visit, what it never records, how long it's kept and how to switch the counting off."
>
  <PageHero
    title="What this site records about your visit."
    accent="records"
    intro="Short version: we count visits without cookies, we never record what you type, and you can switch the counting off below."
  />

  <section class="pb-16 md:pb-24">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-6 md:px-10">
      <div class="max-w-[68ch] text-base md:text-lg text-ink/75 leading-relaxed [&_h2]:text-ink [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:text-xl [&_h2]:md:text-2xl [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:mb-3 [&_p]:mb-4 [&_li]:mb-2 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-5 [&_ul]:mb-4">
        <h2>Counting visits</h2>
        <p>We count visits to this site ourselves, without cookies. We record:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>which pages are opened, and in what order</li>
          <li>where the visit came from (a search engine, a link on another site, a campaign tag)</li>
          <li>whether the screen is phone, tablet or desktop sized</li>
          <li>how far down a page is scrolled and roughly how long it's open</li>
          <li>which links and buttons are used, and that a form was started or sent</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We never record what you type into a form, and the counting stores nothing on your device. Your IP address is turned
          into a code that changes every day and can't be turned back into the address. The address itself is never kept, so
          we can't recognise you from one day to the next.
        </p>
        <p>
          The records stay on our own server, aren't shared with anyone, and are deleted after 14 months. We use them to see
          which pages help and which get in the way.
        </p>
        <p>
          If your browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control, nothing is counted. You can also switch it off
          yourself (that choice is saved in this browser):
        </p>
        <p><button type="button" data-count-switch class={link}>Don’t count my visits in this browser</button></p>

        <h2>The optional analytics cookie</h2>
        <p>
          The banner at the bottom of the site asks whether we can also use Google Analytics. It loads only if you choose
          Accept, and sets one analytics cookie. If you decline, or ignore the banner, it never loads.
        </p>

        <h2>When you get in touch</h2>
        <p>
          If you send the contact form, book a call, ask for a carbon audit or join the newsletter, we keep what you send so we
          can reply and do what you asked. The newsletter only starts once you confirm by email, and every issue has an
          unsubscribe link. The newsletter form is checked by Cloudflare Turnstile to keep bots out.
        </p>

        <h2>Asking about your data</h2>
        <p>
          To see, correct or delete anything we hold about you, email
          <a href="mailto:nathan@oakfox.co.uk" class={link}>nathan@oakfox.co.uk</a>. OakFox is based in West Lancashire, UK.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
